# Myriad (CR 702.116a): "for each opponent other than defending player" - with a single opponent, who is the defending player,
# there is none, so no token is created and nothing is asked (the ruling). The Patrol attacks alone on turn 3 for 1.
# The positive control is the three-player scenario, where the same attack is asked what the token attacks.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Wyrm's Crossing Patrol
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Wyrm's Crossing Patrol.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Wyrm's Crossing Patrol > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Target
? Combat.Attackers.Count = 1
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 2
